WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.762
Last, keeping it honest during
and after the hybrid period.

2
00:00:03.762 --> 00:00:07.788
Chapter 11's troubleshooting
reference covers the common failures.

3
00:00:07.788 --> 00:00:13.978
A private endpoint returning its public
address usually means the privatelink zone

4
00:00:13.978 --> 00:00:18.947
isn't linked to the querying network,
a forwarder targets 168.63.129.16,

5
00:00:18.947 --> 00:00:21.912
or a Windows forwarder times out too soon.

6
00:00:21.912 --> 00:00:26.320
Domain join failing from a cloud VM
means the locator records aren't

7
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:31.513
resolvable from that network, so prove
SRV forwarding before any cloud VM joins.

8
00:00:31.513 --> 00:00:35.037
Queries that never resolve
are usually a forwarding loop.

9
00:00:35.037 --> 00:00:38.863
Old answers after a move are
cached within the old TTL.

10
00:00:38.863 --> 00:00:43.487
And DNSSEC failing after a move means
the parent's DS record wasn't updated.

11
00:00:43.487 --> 00:00:44.874
Watch continuously.

12
00:00:44.874 --> 00:00:48.257
Resolve the locator records
every fifteen minutes

13
00:00:48.257 --> 00:00:51.325
from every site and VNet,
site records included.

14
00:00:51.325 --> 00:00:56.030
Detect drift by normalizing both
sides to name, type and data,

15
00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:01.487
excluding SOA and NS, and commit each
report so the history is evidence.

16
00:01:01.487 --> 00:01:04.675
Report stale-record and
dangling-CNAME rates monthly.

17
00:01:04.675 --> 00:01:08.051
The Private Resolver has no
forwarding-failure metric,

18
00:01:08.051 --> 00:01:11.427
so alert on inbound queries
at zero in business hours or

19
00:01:11.427 --> 00:01:14.950
spiking over two hundred percent,
and use synthetic tests.

20
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:20.702
The evidence checklist opens with the
five decisions, each checked live,

21
00:01:20.702 --> 00:01:26.551
then Protective DNS and encrypted DNS
evidence, IPAM inventory for CM-8,

22
00:01:26.551 --> 00:01:30.194
logs at M-26-14 retention,
rogue DHCP and router

23
00:01:30.194 --> 00:01:34.412
advertisement detection,
and reviewed delegations.

24
00:01:34.412 --> 00:01:37.787
Appendix B maps each
requirement to its evidence.

25
00:01:37.787 --> 00:01:43.142
So, before the next SD-WAN or DDI change:
audit every branch's redirect-dns target,

26
00:01:43.142 --> 00:01:46.766
verify the chain order in
the running configuration,

27
00:01:46.766 --> 00:01:51.380
complete the AD DNS inventory before
touching a domain controller,

28
00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:56.487
confirm the sovereign-cloud limits,
and take open questions to the vendors.

29
00:01:56.487 --> 00:01:58.904
Chapter 09 assigns who does each,

30
00:01:58.904 --> 00:02:03.737
and Chapter 12 measures success
as resolution-path consistency.

31
00:02:03.737 --> 00:02:04.560
Thank you.
